#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tkgenome - GenBank viewer for bacterial genomes, in Python + Tk.

Standard library only.  Opens a GenBank flat file (plain or gzip-compressed)
and shows linked views of the genome:

  * a circular map, position 0 at the top running clockwise; forward-strand
    features on the outer ring, reverse-strand features on the inner ring,
    plus optional GC-content and GC-skew rings and a colour legend;
  * a linear detail strip (gene arrows with labels) for the region around the
    selected feature;
  * a sortable, filterable feature table;
  * a sequence pane: nucleotide / protein (FASTA) and qualifiers of the
    selected feature(s).

Usage:  tkgenome [file.gb | file.gbk.gz]

Mouse (circular map)
  click            select a feature (Ctrl/Cmd-click adds to the selection)
  wheel            zoom about the pointer       drag        pan
  Shift-drag       rotate the circle            double-click on empty space
                   resets the view
  hover            tooltip with the feature's details
Mouse (detail strip)
  click / hover    as above                     wheel       zoom
  drag             pan                          double-click fit the selection
Keys (with the map or strip focused)
  + / -  zoom      0  reset view                Left / Right  pan the strip
Other
  Ctrl/Cmd-O open a file, Ctrl/Cmd-Q quit.  "Go to" takes a coordinate
  (1234567, 1.2m, 500k, 1000-2000) or a gene / locus tag.

Filter box syntax (terms are ANDed, "!" negates):
  dnaA                      substring of id / type / product / gene
  type:CDS  strand:-        feature type, strand
  len>1000  start>=100000   numeric comparison on len, start, end
  product:transpos  EC_number:2.7  note:frameshift   any qualifier
  rec:name                  record name   !pseudo   hide matches
"""

import gzip
import math
